    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened in 1886, with Calvin Skinner as its first postmaster, marking Star’s first federal presence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first public road linking Star to Goldthwaite opened in 1890, opening the town to regional trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By 1895, Star boasted a saloon, several grocery stores, and a drug store, reflecting a bustling frontier economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Early residents ran a store and a gin, providing essential goods and cotton processing for the surrounding farms.",
